    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb099375_c7601115",
        "filename": "voltha/core/logical_device_agent.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000005
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-19T21:47:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Possibly - not sure how it is working in VOLTHA - do we usually allow modification of objects like devices and ports from the northbound interfaces? Or should devices and ports mostly be modified by the adapters only? If we just want to modify the config state of the port then the API should probably just expose that, rather than looking like it allows the entire port to be modified. What are you thoughts on this?",
      "parentUuid": "21d98ae7_90585792",
      "revId": "e21d9e2dbf97eaece7698ea9eab7cc5069804bfa",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b15b15db_2f7cc17f",
        "filename": "voltha/core/logical_device_agent.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-20T01:07:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In voltha we have some access restrictions on the data model whereby some objects/attributes are read only.   Modifications of a device and port depend on the use case.  For example we expose API to reboot/enable/disable a device.   In the OF port context, I would think if the state is changed from UP to DOWN then that would trigger the disable ONU device.   Are there attributes other than config state that would likely be modified by a user?",
      "parentUuid": "eb099375_c7601115",
      "revId": "e21d9e2dbf97eaece7698ea9eab7cc5069804bfa",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb454187_6f492a5e",
        "filename": "voltha/core/logical_device_agent.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000005
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-20T16:53:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No I don\u0027t think so - I think setting the port config is probably the only thing that should be changed by the user, other attributes should be owned by the adapter that created the port. \nHow are the access restrictions recorded?",
      "parentUuid": "b15b15db_2f7cc17f",
      "revId": "e21d9e2dbf97eaece7698ea9eab7cc5069804bfa",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3423eba4_86dad9c7",
        "filename": "voltha/core/logical_device_agent.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-20T17:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The access restrictions (really whether an attribute is read-only or not) is set at the data model layer.  Your can set it in the proto file.  Take a look at the voltha.proto and you will see those \"annotations\".   In this scenario, it may be better to change the voltha API to updateOFPortState rather than update the OF port .",
      "parentUuid": "fb454187_6f492a5e",
      "revId": "e21d9e2dbf97eaece7698ea9eab7cc5069804bfa",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
